    ## The release binaries the corpus and negative runs use
    
    `specs/0013-formulas.md`, "P3", has the part 6 corpus run use the release
    binaries this log hashed, and the negative log run the release
    `probe-emend-formulas-write-xml`. Both are built and hashed in
    `records/logs/m1p6-p3/size.log`: `emend-copy` and `xlsx-diff` in the
    release profile for the host and for i686-unknown-linux-musl, and the probe in the `size`
    profile above, which inherits release. Each is printed there on a line
    `hash: <name> <target> <sha256>`, and the run and negative logs each compare
    the sha256 of what they run with the one this log printed, reading it out of
    this log by command.
    
    ## Reading these figures
    
    File sizes on this target change in whole 4096-byte steps. They are not
    themselves whole pages: all twelve probes leave the same remainder, 2596
    bytes, modulo 4096, so it is every DIFFERENCE between them that is a whole
    number of pages. A change under a page is therefore invisible in the file
    size, while the section totals, from `size -A`, resolve to the byte. Both
    are given for every figure above.
